"""Inline Lucide SVG icons for the sidebar navigation.

The rail used to render <i data-lucide="..."> placeholders next to a
FontAwesome fallback and let lucide.createIcons() swap them in on
DOMContentLoaded. That swap runs AFTER the first paint, so every page
navigation repainted the rail with blank icon slots and filled them in a
moment later — the flash seen in the sidebar screen recording.

Rendering the same Lucide geometry server-side, inline, puts the icons in
the first byte of HTML: first paint equals final paint. Attributes mirror
lucide's own createIcons() output (the default attribute set from
lucide.min.js plus aria-hidden="true", class "lucide lucide-{name}") but
omit data-lucide, so createIcons() leaves these elements untouched.

Geometry generated from static/js/vendor/lucide.min.js — do not hand-edit.
"""
